/* book exam traps: Prokaryotes do organize their DNA: the nucleoid is folded and packed with proteins. What they lack is a nuclear envelope. | Svedberg units do not add up: 30S + 50S gives 70S, and 40S + 60S gives 80S. S measures how fast a particle sinks in a centrifuge, which depends on shape as well as mass. | "Eukaryotes have 80S ribosomes" is true of the cytosol only; their mitochondria and chloroplasts have smaller, bacteria-like ribosomes. | Older books draw mesosomes, membrane infoldings said to carry out respiration. Electron microscopists now regard them as artefacts of chemical fixation; say so if your book shows them. */
